# Hamza Tauqeer — Personal Founder Website

A minimal personal website establishing my digital identity as a founder, builder, and software engineer.

This page serves as my personal corner of the internet — a place to share who I am, what I build, and how I approach software, products, and business.

## Live Websites

- **Cloudflare Workers:** https://me-founder.iamhamzatauqeer.workers.dev/
- **Netlify:** https://hamzatauqeer.netlify.app/

## About

I'm **Hamza Tauqeer**, founder at Idea Section. I've been building software, working with engineering teams, and solving technical and business problems since 2017.

My work revolves around software engineering, product development, AI, systems, and turning ideas into practical solutions.

## Purpose

- Establish a consistent personal identity across the web.
- Build discoverability for my name and founder profile.
- Create a central destination for my professional presence.
- Connect my work, profiles, and future projects.
- Lay the foundation for a more developed personal website.

## Tech Stack

Currently intentionally simple:

- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript (where needed)
- Static deployment

No framework or complex infrastructure is required at this stage.

## Deployment

The website is deployed using:

- Cloudflare Workers
- Netlify

Both deployments currently serve the personal website.

## Roadmap

- [x] Launch the initial personal website
- [x] Deploy to Cloudflare Workers
- [x] Deploy to Netlify
- [ ] Configure Google Search Console
- [ ] Improve SEO metadata and indexing
- [ ] Add Person structured data (JSON-LD)
- [ ] Consolidate around a primary domain
- [ ] Connect professional profiles and projects
- [ ] Migrate to Next.js
- [ ] Build a more dynamic personal platform over time

## Future Direction

The current implementation is a lightweight static page by design. The next iteration is planned to move to **Next.js**, creating a foundation for expanding the website with more structured content, projects, writing, and other personal-brand assets.

The goal is not to overengineer the website today, but to evolve it as the identity and content grow.

